  (text "wiper = clean + b (driven - clean)\nb = 0 clean only, 1 driven only" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 129.54 68.58 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "72138341-7863-556f-9fba-4a0ca3dcbc89"))
  (text "Section 8 of the circuit notes. A clean/driven blend is documented [1]; its circuit is not.\nRVX2, UX5: a linear crossfade (chosen). A pot between two low-impedance sources into a follower gives exactly\nclean + b (driven - clean), the DSP's blend. RX11, RX12: the driven-path trim drvTrim = 0.28 (chosen, matched by\nmeasurement); their 3.7 kOhm source impedance bends the pot's law by a few per cent." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 198.12 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c6ce7d26-323a-5d84-a2c7-e16cef3d2e83"))
